# Laptop Exec — hybrid routing

`~/mounts/` may be STALE for **git** truth. Mount Cursor tools are ALLOWED.

**Priority + failover:** use column 1st when healthy; if unavailable/errors,
use 2nd then 3rd in the **same turn**. Never stuck on a dead path.

## Priority by action (measured 2026-07-26)

| Action | 1st | 2nd (if 1st fails) | 3rd | Parallel |
|--------|-----|--------------------|-----|----------|
| **Read** | Cursor Read on `/mounts/` | windows-mcp `FileSystem` `mode=read` | `laptop-exec read` | mount ~16–32; MCP ~8–12; LE ≤4 |
| **Grep (content)** | Cursor Grep on `/mounts/` | MCP `Select-String` | `laptop-exec rg` | mount ~16–32; SS ~4–8; LE ≤4 |
| **Glob / filename** | windows-mcp FileSystem search/list | Cursor Glob / mount `ls` | `laptop-exec run` | MCP ~8–12; mount ~16 |
| **Write / Edit / …** | windows-mcp FileSystem `mode=write` | Cursor on `/mounts/` | `laptop-exec write` | MCP ~8–10; mount ~10; LE ≤4 |
| **git** | `laptop-exec git` only | — | — | ≤4 LE |
| **Shell build/test** | windows-mcp PowerShell | `laptop-exec run` | mount Shell OK | MCP free / LE ≤4 |
| **UI / Screenshot** | windows-mcp only | — | — | MCP free |

**Failover:** mount STALE/EPERM → MCP → LE. MCP not listed / one hard fail → mount + LE (MCP down for session; never retry same call). Tunnel DOWN → user `connect.bat`/`connect.sh`.

**Notes:** FileSystem search ≠ content Grep. MCP relative → Desktop (use absolute project root). Healthy default: Read/Grep on mount; Write/Glob on MCP.

## Parallel

Fan out independent ops to the caps above. LE hard cap 8 (prefer ≤4).

## Hooks

Read/Grep/Glob/Write/Edit/Shell on `/mounts/` = **ALLOW**. Task = ALLOW (paste PRIORITY+FAILOVER block). Project `hooks.json` = `{"version":1,"hooks":{}}`.

## Paths

- Mount: `/home/$USER/mounts/PROJECT/REL`
- MCP: absolute Windows (`LAPTOP_REMOTE_PATH` / `rpath` + REL)
- LE: `-p PROJECT` + repo-relative. `rg`: no `-i`/`-l`/`-n`/`--glob`

Sudo: `sudo-from-laptop --smart|--sepidz -- …` — never ask for a password.
